    "text": "\n000\nFXUS65 KVEF 222340\nAFDVEF\n\nArea Forecast Discussion\nNational Weather Service Las Vegas NV\n440 PM PDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\n.KEY MESSAGES...\n\n* Scattered showers and thunderstorms with brief heavy rain, small\n  hail, and lightning will remain possible through this evening.\n  \n* Drier conditions and seasonable temperatures expected this \n  weekend and early next week. \n\n&&\n\n.DISCUSSION...through next Thursday.\n\nA large 564dm low continues to slowly meander across central\nCalifornia this afternoon, with a strong and deep southerly flow\nout ahead of it. This flow pattern has entrained some deeper\nsurface moisture north into the region over the past couple days,\nand as the low moves inland today, cooler air aloft is moving in\nhelping to add to the instability present. This is sparking a few\ncorridors of strong thunderstorm activity again this afternoon.\nDeep layer shear of 40-50 knots or greater is resulting in very\nfast northward storm motions which is helping to limit the flood\nthreat, but enhancing the risk of small to potentially quarter\nsized hail. This risk will remain present through the evening\nhours before instability begins to wane and the corridor of\ninstability and wind shear shifts eastward. \n\nBy tomorrow, the low will have moved inland and begun to weaken\nconsiderably, but weak troughing will remain over head with\nlingering terrain driven showers possible. Conditions will\ncontinue to dry through the weekend and next week with\ntemperatures returning to near normal. \n\n&&\n\n.AVIATION...For Harry Reid...For the 00Z Forecast \nPackage...Southwest winds will continue to gust to around 20KT \nthrough about 03Z, at which points gusts should end but expect south \nwinds at 8-10KT through the first part of the night. Lighter winds \narrive between 09Z-12Z when they become light and variable for the \nrest of the night into Friday morning. Winds on Friday will remain \nunder 8KT, becoming east in the afternoon before backing to the \nnorthwest around sunset. There is a low chance for showers and \nthunderstorms early this evening around the area, which could bring \nbrief moderate rainfall, lightning, and CIGs down to 5000ft. By 03Z, \nshowers will diminish and a dry forecast is expected the rest of the \nTAF period. \n\nFor the rest of southern Nevada, northwest Arizona and southeast \nCalifornia...For the 00Z Forecast Package...Scattered showers with \nisolated thunderstorms will persist into the evening, with the \nhighest chances in Inyo County into the Southern Great Basin. \nPrecipitation will end overnight and other than a few showers in the \nterrain of Inyo County on Friday, it will be dry across the region \nthe rest of the TAF period. Southwest winds will continue to gust 20-\n30KT through about sunset, then winds will slowly diminish tonight. \nWInds will drop below 10KT areawide by Friday morning and will \ngenerally remain at or below 10KT through Friday, favoring the north \nto northeast in the afternoon. \n\n&&\n\n.SPOTTER INFORMATION STATEMENT...Spotters are encouraged to report\nany significant weather or impacts according to standard operating\nprocedures.\n\n&&\n\n$$\n\nDISCUSSION...Outler\nAVIATION...Nickerson\n\nFor more forecast information...see us on our webpage:\nhttps://weather.gov/lasvegas or follow us on Facebook and Twitter\n",
